-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/11 (17.7.2024): קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ד,
-- קצובת ביגוד לעובדי הוראה בחינוך הגופני ובחינוך הטכנולוגי
-- The clothing allowance for התשפ"ד: who is entitled, its level and
-- amount, pro-rating by position and across employers, the caps on the
-- scope of employment; the additional allowance of physical-education
-- teachers by their employment rate; and the shoes and coats of teachers
-- and instructors in technological education, by profession.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time for the payment duties is counted in SALARY MONTHS from June 2024's
-- (0): July 2024's salary is 1.
`July 2024's salary` MEANS 1

-- What the employer does: pay each of the three allowances.
DECLARE `clothing action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the clothing allowance` HAS `clothing paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the physical-education allowance` HAS `PE paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the technological-education allowance` HAS `technology paid` IS A NUMBER

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/11 — קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ד`

-- akn:preamble The circular's number, letterhead, footer, date, reference number, addressees (the owners of educational institutions), greeting, subject line and its list of the three subjects below; no rule.

§§ `1 קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ד`

-- akn:art_1/p1 The heading "תחולה" over the applicability paragraph; no rule of its own.
-- akn:art_1/p4 The heading "כללי" over the paragraphs below; no rule of its own.

@desc A teaching employee at one employer in התשפ"ד, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `employee for the clothing allowance` HAS
    `graded on the teaching employees' scale`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc graded on the teaching employees' grading (דירוג עובדי הוראה)
    `employed by an owner under Ministry supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by an owner the Ministry of Education supervises
    `position fraction here`                          IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position at THIS employer (1 = full)
    `physical-education employment rate`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position in which the employee teaches physical education (0 if none)
    `technological-education position fraction`      IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position in technological education or as a professional instructor (0 if none)
    `technological profession`                        IS A `technological profession` @desc the profession taught in technological education

@ref akn:art_1/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 applies to` e IF
        e's `graded on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND e's `employed by an owner under Ministry supervision`

-- 1ב: by the Treasury's instructions (the lead-in), an employee on the
-- teaching scale is entitled to the clothing allowance customary for
-- civil servants who serve the public, for the school year 09/23–08/24.
-- 1ג: at level 4, i.e. ₪2,405.
@ref akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the clothing allowance` e IF
    `section 1 applies to` e

@ref akn:art_1__para_c
`the clothing allowance level` MEANS 4
@ref akn:art_1__para_c
`the full clothing allowance` MEANS 2405

-- 1ד: in proportion to the position, and for no more than one full
-- position. 1ה: at several employers totalling more than 100%, each pays
-- in proportion to the position at it — so the cap is per employer.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the clothing allowance` e IS
    IF `entitled to the clothing allowance` e
    THEN `the full clothing allowance` TIMES min 1 (e's `position fraction here`)
    ELSE 0

-- 1ו: the caps on the scope of employment across all employers.
DECLARE `employment terms` IS ONE OF
    `before the reforms`
    `Oz LaTmura`
    `Ofek Hadash`

DECLARE `post` IS ONE OF
    `teacher`
    `principal`
    `first deputy principal`

@ref akn:art_1__para_f akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_1 akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_2 akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_3
GIVEN t IS AN `employment terms`, p IS A `post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the scope cap in 1ו` t p IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `before the reforms` THEN
        CONSIDER p
        WHEN `principal` THEN 1.5
        OTHERWISE 1.4
    WHEN `Oz LaTmura` THEN
        CONSIDER p
        WHEN `principal` THEN 1
        OTHERWISE 1.25
    WHEN `Ofek Hadash` THEN
        CONSIDER p
        WHEN `teacher` THEN 1.17
        OTHERWISE 1

-- 1ו.3's second paragraph: the caps are subject to the procedure for
-- exceptional employment for התשפ"ד (mokarshimorishmi.pdf), not restated
-- in the circular — whether it permits an employment is an input.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f__subpara_3/p2
GIVEN t IS AN `employment terms`, p IS A `post`, `total scope` IS A NUMBER,
      `the exceptional-employment procedure permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the procedure for exceptional employment for התשפ"ד permits this employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is within the caps` t p `total scope` `the exceptional-employment procedure permits it` IF
        `total scope` AT MOST `the scope cap in 1ו` t p
    OR `the exceptional-employment procedure permits it`

-- The closing paragraph restates the caps "(140% without a reform, 117% in
-- Ofek Hadash and 125% in Oz LaTmura)" as no change in the conditions for
-- approval and no permission beyond them. F-2023-24_tashpad_11-a: it gives
-- 140% for everyone outside the reforms, where 1ו.1 gives a principal
-- outside the reforms 150%.
@ref akn:art_1/p5
GIVEN t IS AN `employment terms`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the scope cap as restated` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `before the reforms` THEN 1.4
    WHEN `Oz LaTmura` THEN 1.25
    WHEN `Ofek Hadash` THEN 1.17

`the restated caps differ from 1ו.1 for a principal outside the reforms` MEANS
    NOT (`the scope cap as restated` `before the reforms` EQUALS `the scope cap in 1ו` `before the reforms` `principal`)
#ASSERT `the restated caps differ from 1ו.1 for a principal outside the reforms`

-- The reading adopted (F-2023-24_tashpad_11-a): 1ו.1's specific cap for a
-- principal stands; the restatement is read as the teachers' caps — it is
-- the caps of 1ו, posts aside, that `the employment is within the caps` applies.

@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `the clothing allowance is paid in July 2024` e IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the clothing allowance` c PROVIDED c EQUALS `the clothing allowance` e
    WITHIN `July 2024's salary`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1א: the clothing allowance is paid in full in July 2024's salary"

§§ `2 קצובת ביגוד נוספת למורה לחינוך גופני`

-- Section 2: an allowance in addition to the general one (it covers the
-- purchase of sun protection), updating the amounts of circular תשע"ב/8 by
-- the table, by the employment rate. F-2023-24_tashpad_11-b: "שיעור
-- העסקה" may be the employee's whole employment or the part of it in
-- physical education; for a full-position teacher who teaches physical
-- education in a part of it, they give different rows. The reading adopted:
-- the part in physical education, the way 3.3 pro-rates the technological
-- allowance by the position in technological education.
DECLARE `PE row` HAS
    `from rate`             IS A NUMBER
    `from rate included`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `to rate`               IS A NUMBER
    `to rate included`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `PE amount`             IS A NUMBER

-- The table as printed: below a third (0); from a third to a half,
-- inclusive (767); above a half (1,530).
@ref akn:art_2/p1 akn:art_2/p2 akn:art_2/t1
`the physical-education table` MEANS
    LIST `PE row` 0   TRUE  (1 DIVIDED BY 3) FALSE 0,
         `PE row` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) TRUE 0.5 TRUE 767,
         `PE row` 0.5 FALSE 99  TRUE 1530

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER, row IS A `PE row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rate falls in` r row IF
        (    r GREATER THAN row's `from rate`
         OR (row's `from rate included` AND r EQUALS row's `from rate`))
    AND (    r LESS THAN row's `to rate`
         OR (row's `to rate included` AND r EQUALS row's `to rate`))

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the PE amounts for rate` r IS
    map (GIVEN row YIELD row's `PE amount`)
        (filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the rate falls in` r row) `the physical-education table`)

-- Every rate falls in exactly one row, the bounds included.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD count (`the PE amounts for rate` r) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 0, 0.1, 0.3333, 1 DIVIDED BY 3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.5001, 0.75, 1, 1.4)

@ref akn:art_2/t1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the physical-education allowance` e IS
    IF `section 1 applies to` e
    THEN CONSIDER `the PE amounts for rate` (e's `physical-education employment rate`)
         WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN a
         OTHERWISE 0
    ELSE 0

GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the physical-education allowance by the whole position` e IS
    CONSIDER `the PE amounts for rate` (e's `position fraction here`)
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN a
    OTHERWISE 0

`a full-position teacher teaching physical education in 40%` MEANS
    `employee for the clothing allowance` WITH
        `graded on the teaching employees' scale`         IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner under Ministry supervision` IS TRUE
        `position fraction here`                          IS 1
        `physical-education employment rate`              IS 0.4
        `technological-education position fraction`      IS 0
        `technological profession`                        IS `another profession`

`the employment rate read two ways gives two PE rows` MEANS
    NOT (`the physical-education allowance` `a full-position teacher teaching physical education in 40%`
         EQUALS `the physical-education allowance by the whole position` `a full-position teacher teaching physical education in 40%`)
#ASSERT `the employment rate read two ways gives two PE rows`

§§ `3 קצובת ביגוד בחינוך הטכנולוגי`

@desc The professions of section 3.1's two lists, and any other.
DECLARE `technological profession` IS ONE OF
    `aviation systems`
    `mechatronics`
    `technical marine thermodynamics`
    `CAD/CAM systems`
    `maintenance of mechanical systems`
    `motor-vehicle mechanics systems`
    `computerised vehicle systems`
    `power, command and control systems`
    `climate-control systems`
    `hotel cookery and baking`
    `seamanship – ships`
    `television and film systems`
    `photography systems`
    `electronic systems`
    `computing and control systems`
    `computer systems`
    `systems design and programming`
    `biotechnology systems`
    `tourism management`
    `hotel management`
    `early-childhood education`
    `design`
    `fashion and costume`
    `hairdressing and beauty care`
    `nursing`
    `applied art`
    `another profession`

-- 3.1א: a pair of shoes and two coats a year.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a/t1
`the shoes-and-coats professions` MEANS
    LIST `aviation systems`, `mechatronics`, `technical marine thermodynamics`,
         `CAD/CAM systems`, `maintenance of mechanical systems`,
         `motor-vehicle mechanics systems`, `computerised vehicle systems`,
         `power, command and control systems`, `climate-control systems`,
         `hotel cookery and baking`, `seamanship – ships`,
         `television and film systems`, `photography systems`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a/p2
`the value of a pair of shoes and two coats` MEANS 631

-- 3.1ב: two coats a year.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b/t1
`the two-coats professions` MEANS
    LIST `electronic systems`, `computing and control systems`, `computer systems`,
         `systems design and programming`, `biotechnology systems`,
         `tourism management`, `hotel management`, `early-childhood education`,
         `design`, `fashion and costume`, `hairdressing and beauty care`,
         `nursing`, `applied art`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b/p2
`the value of two coats` MEANS 392

-- No profession is in both lists.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD NOT elem p `the two-coats professions`) `the shoes-and-coats professions`
#ASSERT count `the shoes-and-coats professions` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT count `the two-coats professions` EQUALS 13

@ref akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_a akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_b
GIVEN p IS A `technological profession`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full technological allowance for` p IS
    IF elem p `the shoes-and-coats professions`
    THEN `the value of a pair of shoes and two coats`
    ELSE IF elem p `the two-coats professions`
         THEN `the value of two coats`
         ELSE 0

-- 3.2: in addition to the general clothing allowance. 3.3: in proportion
-- to the position in technological education, for no more than one full
-- position.
@ref akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2 akn:art_3__para_3-3
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the technological-education allowance` e IS
    IF `section 1 applies to` e
    THEN `the full technological allowance for` (e's `technological profession`)
         TIMES min 1 (e's `technological-education position fraction`)
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_2/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `all clothing allowances` e IS
    `the clothing allowance` e
    PLUS `the physical-education allowance` e
    PLUS `the technological-education allowance` e

-- F-2023-24_tashpad_11-c: section 1א dates the payment of the general
-- allowance (July 2024's salary); sections 2 and 3 say "יש לשלם" and name
-- no month. The reading adopted: they are paid with the general allowance,
-- in July 2024's salary.
@ref akn:art_2/t1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `the physical-education allowance is paid` e IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the physical-education allowance` c PROVIDED c EQUALS `the physical-education allowance` e
    WITHIN `July 2024's salary`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2: the additional allowance of a physical-education teacher (read as paid with the general allowance)"

`section 1 names a payment month` MEANS TRUE
`section 2 names a payment month` MEANS FALSE
`section 3 names a payment month` MEANS FALSE
`sections 2 and 3 name no payment month` MEANS
    `section 1 names a payment month` AND (NOT `section 2 names a payment month`) AND (NOT `section 3 names a payment month`)
#ASSERT `sections 2 and 3 name no payment month`

@ref akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee for the clothing allowance`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `the technological-education allowance is paid` e IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the technological-education allowance` c PROVIDED c EQUALS `the technological-education allowance` e
    WITHIN `July 2024's salary`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 3: the clothing allowance in technological education (read as paid with the general allowance)"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the signatures and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples, on the circular's own amounts.
`a mechatronics teacher on a 1.2 position, 0.5 of it in technology` MEANS
    `employee for the clothing allowance` WITH
        `graded on the teaching employees' scale`         IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner under Ministry supervision` IS TRUE
        `position fraction here`                          IS 1.2
        `physical-education employment rate`              IS 0
        `technological-education position fraction`      IS 0.5
        `technological profession`                        IS `mechatronics`

#ASSERT `the clothing allowance` `a mechatronics teacher on a 1.2 position, 0.5 of it in technology` EQUALS 2405
#ASSERT `the technological-education allowance` `a mechatronics teacher on a 1.2 position, 0.5 of it in technology` EQUALS 315.5
#ASSERT `the physical-education allowance` `a full-position teacher teaching physical education in 40%` EQUALS 767
#ASSERT `the PE amounts for rate` 0.3 EQUALS LIST 0
#ASSERT `the PE amounts for rate` 0.6 EQUALS LIST 1530
#ASSERT `the full technological allowance for` `nursing` EQUALS 392
#ASSERT `the employment is within the caps` `Oz LaTmura` `principal` 1 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the employment is within the caps` `Oz LaTmura` `principal` 1.1 FALSE

#TRACE `the clothing allowance is paid in July 2024` `a mechatronics teacher on a 1.2 position, 0.5 of it in technology` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the clothing allowance` 2405 AT 1
#TRACE `the technological-education allowance is paid` `a mechatronics teacher on a 1.2 position, 0.5 of it in technology` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the technological-education allowance` 315.5 AT 1
#TRACE `the physical-education allowance is paid` `a full-position teacher teaching physical education in 40%` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the physical-education allowance` 767 AT 1
